Concern
Clarification / Impact Mitigation
WebSocket reliability
 The current design does not use WebSockets. We use a controller reconciliation loop (every syncIntervalSeconds) per CR. This avoids long-lived fragile socket connections.
Scaling issues
we are using a single Operator handles all CRs, pulling secrets periodically and injecting them as volumes. This reduces memory/CPU overhead per Pod.
CRD controller complexity
While CRD-based logic exists, it's centralized, manageable, and native to Kubernetes patterns. 
Observability
Pull-based logic is easier to trace — logs are emitted per CR per sync, with standard INFO and ERROR levels. No complex socket tracing is needed.
Vendor/infra compatibility
Pull-model works cleanly behind proxies, NAT, or OpenShift ingress — since it uses simple K8s watch + HTTP(s), no WebSockets involved.
CVE/Upgrades
Our Operator uses only standard SDK (Java Operator SDK 5+) and Fabric8 client. We track upstream CVEs via GitHub dependabot alerts and Operator SDK releases.

